# REGISTRATION.patch — intended shared-file hunks for @ezxomp/gsd-graph 0.1.0-ezxomp.0

Integration owner applies these in one serialized wave. Workers MUST NOT edit
the shared files directly (parallel-agent protocol).

## 1. `.omp-plugin/marketplace.json` — append to `plugins[]`

```json
{
  "name": "gsd-graph",
  "source": "./plugins/gsd-graph",
  "description": "GSD knowledge graph and workflow execution graph (GRAPH.yaml engine) for OMP, ported from gsd-pi.",
  "version": "0.1.0-ezxomp.0",
  "attribution": "Port of gsd-pi graph subsystems (workflow GRAPH.yaml engine + TS-native knowledge graph) to OMP."
}
```

Context: last entry currently `pstack-suite` (alphabetical order is not
enforced; keep existing order, append at end).

## 2. `test/manifest.test.ts` — extend EXPECTED arrays

```ts
EXPECTED_PLUGINS:      add "gsd-graph" (after "pstack-suite")
EXPECTED_PACKAGE_IDS:  "gsd-graph": "@ezxomp/gsd-graph",
EXPECTED_VERSIONS:     "gsd-graph": "0.1.0-ezxomp.0",
```

Smoke sketch (test/smoke-plugins.test.ts):

```ts
describe("smoke: gsd-graph extension entry", () => {
	test("gsd-graph entry registers the declared surface", () => {
		const pkg = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(PLUGINS, "gsd-graph", "package.json"), "utf-8"));
		for (const ext of pkg.omp?.extensions ?? []) {
			const content = readFileSync(join(PLUGINS, "gsd-graph", ext), "utf-8");
			expect(content).toContain('setLabel("GSD Graph")');
			// Tools live in src/tools.ts, not the entry file — assert names there.
			const toolContent = readFileSync(join(PLUGINS, "gsd-graph", "src", "tools.ts"), "utf-8");
			expect(toolContent).toContain('"gsd_graph"');
			expect(toolContent).toContain('"gsd_graph_run"');
			// command: /gsd-graph
			expect(content).toContain('registerGsdGraphCommand');
			// session_start autoRebuild hook
			expect(content).toContain('session_start');
		}
	});
});
```

(Also safe to add `"gsd-graph"` to the existing smoke registration-slugs and
cross-plugin tool-name-uniqueness slug lists — the plugin declares exactly two
tools, `gsd_graph` and `gsd_graph_run`, plus the `/gsd-graph` command and a
`session_start` autoRebuild hook; no name collisions with the other plugins.)

